#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Speed, the zoom buttons back in the view row, plainer Climate TRACE dots,
OpenStreetMap detail on the outlines, and no circle over Eyes.

- Zoom in, zoom out, the compass and the whole-world button sit two by two in
  the view row, between Globe / Flat map and Leave Earth. The legend is full
  width again.
- The "back to the map" circle over Earth in Eyes is gone (Eyes is NASA's
  page, so this map cannot tell how far it is zoomed); the Back to the map
  button stays.
- Climate TRACE and the Cerulean points: plain small dots, one size per zoom,
  no rim.
- Country outlines: from zoom 3.5 CARTO's dark OpenStreetMap basemap (roads,
  rivers, towns, no names) fades in under the labels.
- Speed: the map draws at most 1.5 pixels per screen pixel (half the work on a
  Retina screen), with no cross-fades; no point sorting. With 3D terrain on,
  heights stop at zoom 12 and the Esri relief layer is put away.

Needs patch_eyes_cerulean.py first.
Run from the repo root:  python3 patch_speed_row.py
"""
import pathlib
import sys

